Sun Jet International
For your safety
If you are sitting in an exit row please identify yourself to a crew member to allow for reseating if: You lack the ability to
read, speak, or understand English, or the graphic form, or the ability to understand oral crew commands or hand signals.
Pour votre sécurité
Si votre siège se trouve dans une rangée de sortie veuillez vous identifier aupès d'un membre de l'equipage pour que
vous changiez de siège si vous ne pouvez lire, parler, ou comprendre l'anglais ou le formulaire graphique, ou si vous ne
pouvez pas comprendre des commandes orales ou des signes venant des membres de l'equipage.
Para su seguridad
Si usted está sentado en una hilera de salida, favor de identificarse con algún miembro de la tripulación a fin de permitirle
cambiar de asiento si: Usted no tiene habilidad para leer, hablar o entender el inglés o los gráficos, o habilidad para
entender las órdenes verbales de la tripulación o seffales de mano.
Für ihre sicherheit
Wenn Sie in einer Reihe sitzen, in der sich ein Notausgang befindet, werden Sie gebeten, sich an ein Mitglied des
Flugpersonals zu wenden, damit Ihnen ein anderer Sitzplatz zugewiesen werden kann, falls Sie weder Englisch lesen,
sprechen oder verstehen, noch den Zeichendarstellungen, mündlichen Anweisungen oder Handsignalen folgen können.
Emergency exits are often heavy, awkward to lift, push, pull, and maneuver when opening. Because of this, and
for the benefit of all passengers, Federal Law requires that only consenting, able-bodied passengers, sit in a row
of seats next to an exit. If you are sitting in an exit row, you may be asked to open the exit and assist our crew in the
event of an emergency.
IF YOU ARE SITTING IN AN EXIT ROW PLEASE ASK TO BE RESEATED IF YOU ARE UNABLE TO PERFORM THE
FUNCTIONS SHOWN ON THIS CARD BECAUSE.
•You lack sufficient mobility, strength, or dexterity on both arms and hands, and both legs to:
-Reach upward, sideways, and downward to the location of emergency exit and exit slide operating mechanisms;
-Grasp and push, pull, turn, or otherwise manipulate those mechanisms;
-Push, shove, pull, or otherwise open emergency exits;
-Lift out, hold, and throw overwing exit door hatch through the opening onto wing;
-Remove obstructions similar in size and weight to over-wing exit doors;
-Reach the emergency exit expeditiously;
-Maintain balance while removing obstructions;
-Exit expeditiously;
-Stabilize an escape slide after deployment, or;
-Assist others in getting off an escape slide;
•You are less than 15 years of age or lack the capacity to perform one or more of the applicable functions shown on this
card without the assistance of an adult companion, parent, or other relative;
•You lack sufficient visual capacity to perform one or more of the applicable functions shown on this card without the
assistance of visual aids beyond contact lenses or eye glasses;
•You lack sufficient aural capacity to hear and understand instructions shouted by crew members without the assistance
beyond a hearing aid;
•You lack the ability adequately to impart information orally to other passengers;
•You have a condition or responsibility, such as caring for small children, that might prevent you from performing one or
more of the applicable functions;
•You have a condition that might cause yourself harm if you perform one or more of the applicable functions.
IT IS NOT NECESSARY TO DISCLOSE THE REASON FOR REQUESTING RESEATING.
Federal law requires that all passengers, regardless of where they are sitting or
their physical condition, must review this important information.
Follow these instructions, the directions of the crew, and posted signs.
Please do not remove this card from the aircraft.
